Core/Jessie: Must’ve been hell fixing that radio tower alone.
Core/Rose: I had to. When the grid went down, I couldn’t… I couldn’t reach anyone.
Core/Rose: My family was still out here somewhere. In the suburbs.
Core/Jessie: …Rose…
Core/Rose: I looked for themote a designated st. For weeks. But the streets were already—
Core/Rose: The radio was the only thing I could still fix.
Core/Jessie: For what it’s worth… I’m glad you did.
Core/Rose: Me too.